-- Course catalogue: categories, the 12 programmes from "Our Programs" (fees,
-- 3-month duration, 50/50 instalments) and, for every programme with a Udemy
-- course, the curriculum scraped from that course plus its Udemy bonus card.
--
-- Generated 2026-10-06 from the Udemy public API. Udemy housekeeping (downloads,
-- quizzes, discounts, "join our group" lectures) is left out. Udemy has no
-- module descriptions and almost no lesson descriptions, so those are empty.
--
-- Agentic AI: 26 modules, 182 lessons
-- Generative AI: 55 modules, 258 lessons
-- AI/ML: 63 modules, 456 lessons
-- Data Science: 19 modules, 344 lessons
-- Data Analytics: 8 modules, 174 lessons
-- Python: 100 modules, 625 lessons
-- MERN Stack Development: 34 modules, 353 lessons
-- Frontend Development: 22 modules, 197 lessons
-- Backend Development: 21 modules, 214 lessons
-- Cyber Security: Ethical Hacking: 23 modules, 219 lessons
-- UI/UX Designing: 24 modules, 112 lessons
-- Graphics Designing: 38 modules, 233 lessons
--
-- Runs once per database (tracked in private.seed_log), after seed.sql. On
-- that run it REPLACES the curriculum, instalments and Udemy bonus of these
-- courses, and the AWS course is set to draft (it is not in Our Programs).
-- Thumbnails, benefits, instructors and FAQs are left alone. A second part
-- below replaces these courses' tools the same way.

-- Also created by seed.sql; repeated here so this file can be run on its own.
create table if not exists private.seed_log (
  name text primary key,
  ran_at timestamptz not null default now()
);

do $seed$ begin
  if not exists (select 1 from private.seed_log where name = 'catalogue:2026-10-06') then

    on conflict (id) do update set
      name = excluded.name, short_name = excluded.short_name, slug = excluded.slug,
      description = excluded.description, display_order = excluded.display_order, is_active = true;

    -- learning_mode and is_featured only apply to new rows; existing rows keep what the admin set.

You start with the Python, Pydantic and LangChain foundations, and work with both OpenAI and local Ollama models. From there you move into LangGraph: state, nodes and edges, workflow patterns, human-in-the-loop approval, RAG, guardrails and debugging with LangSmith. Later modules cover the Model Context Protocol (MCP), Claude Code and deep agents.

The second half is project work. You build end-to-end agentic applications, including a chatbot with web search, an AI news summarizer and a blog-generation app, so you finish with working projects for your portfolio.', 12000, null, '3 months', 'hybrid', true, now() - interval '13 minutes'),
      ('20a70350-dffd-40d5-87ad-a61e7360e743', '6ce7e45e-a8cb-4386-8c89-407261d3e2d1', 'Generative AI', 'generative-ai', 'Build generative AI apps with LangChain and Hugging Face: chatbots, RAG, summarisation, fine-tuning and deployment.', 'This course takes you from the foundations of NLP to building and deploying complete generative AI applications. It covers how modern language models work and, more importantly, how to put them to use in real software.

The first part builds the groundwork: Python, machine learning for NLP, and deep learning models such as RNNs, LSTMs, encoder-decoder networks, attention and transformers. You then move to LangChain with OpenAI, Ollama, Groq and Hugging Face models, and learn retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), vector and graph databases, agents, LangGraph and MCP.

Most of the course is hands-on. You build chatbots with memory, chat-with-PDF and chat-with-SQL apps, a search agent, text and YouTube summarisers and a code assistant, fine-tune an LLM, and deploy apps to Streamlit and Hugging Face Spaces.', 12000, null, '3 months', 'online', false, now() - interval '12 minutes'),
      ('d523ab0a-33e1-4928-8734-3956c6739d04', '6ce7e45e-a8cb-4386-8c89-407261d3e2d1', 'AI/ML', 'ai-ml', 'Learn machine learning, deep learning and NLP, from Python and statistics through to deployed end-to-end projects.', 'A complete path into artificial intelligence and machine learning, from your first line of Python to deployed models. It suits beginners as well as anyone who wants to understand both how the algorithms work and how to use them in practice.

You begin with Python, data analysis, and the statistics and probability that machine learning rests on. Then you work through the main algorithms one at a time, each with its intuition and a practical implementation: linear and logistic regression, support vector machines, Naive Bayes, KNN, decision trees, random forests, boosting, and unsupervised methods such as PCA, K-means and DBSCAN.

Later modules cover deep learning (ANNs, RNNs, LSTMs and transformers), NLP, and MLOps: Docker, Git, MLflow, ETL pipelines and deployment to AWS and Azure. Along the way you complete several end-to-end projects.', 12000, null, '3 months', 'physical', false, now() - interval '11 minutes'),
      ('a626064a-7374-423e-86d6-1f8797f54a7c', '4527f811-674e-4998-8dbf-3774355570bd', 'Data Science', 'data-science', 'Go from Python basics to a data science portfolio with pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, scikit-learn and TensorFlow.', 'This course follows the full data science workflow, from setting up your environment to presenting results to stakeholders. If you are new to programming you start with the Python modules; if you already code, you can go straight to the data work.

You learn to explore and clean data with pandas and NumPy, visualise it with Matplotlib, and build machine learning models with scikit-learn. Two milestone projects apply this to classification and to time-series prediction. You then move on to neural networks and transfer learning with TensorFlow, and get an overview of data engineering tools such as Hadoop, Spark and Kafka.

The course closes with how to present your work clearly, and you leave with a portfolio of data science projects.', 12000, null, '3 months', 'hybrid', true, now() - interval '10 minutes'),
      ('85a42f2c-5670-429b-8c72-f5a4e7494af2', '4527f811-674e-4998-8dbf-3774355570bd', 'Data Analytics', 'data-analytics', 'Analyse and visualise data with Python, pandas, NumPy and Matplotlib, and present your findings clearly.', 'Data analysts turn raw data into answers people can act on. This course teaches that work with Python and its core data libraries, starting from the basics, so no programming experience is needed.

You set up a professional data environment and learn Python, then spend most of the course on practical analysis: loading, cleaning and reshaping data with pandas, working with arrays in NumPy, and building clear charts with Matplotlib. You also learn how data is stored and moved at scale, and where analytics fits alongside data engineering.

The final module is about communication: how to present an analysis to managers and stakeholders so that your findings lead to decisions.', 10000, null, '3 months', 'online', false, now() - interval '9 minutes'),
      ('e919197f-2908-5216-8c7b-0d4119158dbe', '370e1495-3ea7-590c-917c-f9664fa01827', 'Python', 'python', 'Learn Python by building 100 projects in 100 days, from games and automation to web apps and data science.', 'This course teaches Python through daily practice. Each day introduces a new concept and ends with a project that uses it, so by the end you have built a portfolio of around 100 programs. No programming experience is needed.

The beginner days cover variables, data types, control flow, loops, functions and dictionaries, with small games such as Hangman, Blackjack and a number-guessing game. The intermediate days introduce object-oriented programming, graphics and desktop apps with Turtle and Tkinter, file handling and APIs, and build games such as Snake and Pong.

From there you move into professional work: web scraping with Beautiful Soup and Selenium, automation, web development with Flask, databases with SQLAlchemy, and data science with pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib and scikit-learn. The last days are portfolio projects that you plan and build on your own.', 8000, null, '3 months', 'hybrid', false, now() - interval '8 minutes'),
      ('f42af617-4d01-4006-888b-4d6d6b6052f4', 'a3394a82-6db1-422e-882a-e12dcf5a4969', 'MERN Stack Development', 'mern-stack-development', 'Become a full-stack JavaScript developer with HTML, CSS, Tailwind, React, Node.js, Express and MongoDB.', 'This course takes you from the basics of the web to building and deploying complete full-stack applications. It is built around the MERN stack (MongoDB, Express, React and Node.js) and the tools professional teams use alongside it.

You start with HTML, CSS, Tailwind CSS and JavaScript, practising each with hands-on challenges and small JavaScript projects, and learn Git and GitHub for version control. The backend modules cover Node.js, Express and MongoDB, including authentication, a large backend project and aggregation pipelines, plus SQL with MySQL and PostgreSQL.

On the frontend you build ten React projects, then move to Next.js for full-stack apps. Later modules cover deployment, Docker, event-driven architecture, the Fastify framework, an AI-powered SaaS app with Prisma, a learning management system with a payment gateway, and an AI code editor.', 10000, null, '3 months', 'hybrid', true, now() - interval '7 minutes'),
      ('a31d768d-750b-4607-8c8d-6cd1a8b5994b', 'a3394a82-6db1-422e-882a-e12dcf5a4969', 'Frontend Development', 'frontend-development', 'Course details coming soon.', '', 8000, null, '3 months', 'online', false, now() - interval '6 minutes'),
      ('8ddf1088-14f1-46d0-827a-17b814c7539f', 'a3394a82-6db1-422e-882a-e12dcf5a4969', 'Backend Development', 'backend-development', 'Course details coming soon.', '', 8000, null, '3 months', 'online', false, now() - interval '5 minutes'),
      ('f7b2c938-f077-4b4c-8b37-73eb73e758f3', '5df8a66f-8525-45e6-8ead-3d9ddfc14c16', 'Cyber Security: Ethical Hacking', 'ethical-hacking', 'Course details coming soon.', '', 8000, null, '3 months', 'online', false, now() - interval '4 minutes'),
      ('74b2aa62-017d-4a09-88bc-1c1565e2b715', '4ebda519-dcbf-4c71-80b9-f10eaad863df', 'UI/UX Designing', 'ui-ux-design', 'Design websites and mobile apps in Figma, from briefs and wireframes to interactive prototypes and developer hand-off.', 'This course teaches the UI/UX design process in Figma, the tool most product teams use today. It is aimed at beginners, so you don''t need any design experience to start.

You begin with a client brief and a user persona, then create low-fidelity wireframes. From there you learn to use colour, type, icons and images well, and to build reusable UI with components, variants, auto layout and constraints. You also make interactive prototypes with animations and micro-interactions, and test them on your phone.

Each topic comes with a short class project, and you finish with a complete design taken from the brief to a style guide and production-ready assets for developers.', 7000, null, '3 months', 'hybrid', true, now() - interval '3 minutes'),
      ('1e73e4b8-99b3-40f3-8d02-fae509493379', '0c89dd00-d674-4fa6-82a6-f93e17ec9dd8', 'Graphics Designing', 'graphic-design', 'Learn design theory, Photoshop, Illustrator and InDesign, and create logos, brand identities and print layouts.', 'This course gives you a solid grounding in graphic design: the theory that makes a design work, and the Adobe tools used to produce it. It starts from the basics and suits complete beginners.

You study typography, colour, layout and the history of design styles, then learn Adobe Photoshop for photo editing, manipulation and AI tools such as Generative Fill. In Adobe Illustrator you work with vectors, the pen tool and 3D effects, and in InDesign you build multi-page layouts.

The course is project-based: a double-exposure effect, a YouTube thumbnail, a book cover, a logo and brand identity with presentation mockups, and a cookbook layout. It also covers giving and receiving feedback, current design trends and finding your design niche.', 7000, null, '3 months', 'physical', false, now() - interval '2 minutes')
    on conflict (id) do update set
      category_id = excluded.category_id, name = excluded.name, slug = excluded.slug,
      short_description = case when excluded.description = '' then courses.short_description else excluded.short_description end,
      description = case when excluded.description = '' then courses.description else excluded.description end,
      actual_price = excluded.actual_price, discount_price = null, duration = excluded.duration,
      created_at = excluded.created_at;

    update public.courses set status = 'published' where id in ('7516a9d7-d1dd-42c8-8c5f-53cea00ed33c', '20a70350-dffd-40d5-87ad-a61e7360e743', 'd523ab0a-33e1-4928-8734-3956c6739d04', 'a626064a-7374-423e-86d6-1f8797f54a7c', '85a42f2c-5670-429b-8c72-f5a4e7494af2', 'e919197f-2908-5216-8c7b-0d4119158dbe', 'f42af617-4d01-4006-888b-4d6d6b6052f4', 'a31d768d-750b-4607-8c8d-6cd1a8b5994b', '8ddf1088-14f1-46d0-827a-17b814c7539f', 'f7b2c938-f077-4b4c-8b37-73eb73e758f3', '74b2aa62-017d-4a09-88bc-1c1565e2b715', '1e73e4b8-99b3-40f3-8d02-fae509493379');
    -- The page builds its curriculum PDF from the modules below; the old sample PDF no longer matches.
    update public.courses set curriculum_pdf_url = null where id in ('7516a9d7-d1dd-42c8-8c5f-53cea00ed33c', '20a70350-dffd-40d5-87ad-a61e7360e743', 'd523ab0a-33e1-4928-8734-3956c6739d04', 'a626064a-7374-423e-86d6-1f8797f54a7c', '85a42f2c-5670-429b-8c72-f5a4e7494af2', 'e919197f-2908-5216-8c7b-0d4119158dbe', 'f42af617-4d01-4006-888b-4d6d6b6052f4', '74b2aa62-017d-4a09-88bc-1c1565e2b715', '1e73e4b8-99b3-40f3-8d02-fae509493379');
    update public.courses set status = 'draft' where id = '420ccfc3-75a4-41cd-868f-69770e2ad8df';

    delete from public.course_installments where course_id in ('7516a9d7-d1dd-42c8-8c5f-53cea00ed33c', '20a70350-dffd-40d5-87ad-a61e7360e743', 'd523ab0a-33e1-4928-8734-3956c6739d04', 'a626064a-7374-423e-86d6-1f8797f54a7c', '85a42f2c-5670-429b-8c72-f5a4e7494af2', 'e919197f-2908-5216-8c7b-0d4119158dbe', 'f42af617-4d01-4006-888b-4d6d6b6052f4', 'a31d768d-750b-4607-8c8d-6cd1a8b5994b', '8ddf1088-14f1-46d0-827a-17b814c7539f', 'f7b2c938-f077-4b4c-8b37-73eb73e758f3', '74b2aa62-017d-4a09-88bc-1c1565e2b715', '1e73e4b8-99b3-40f3-8d02-fae509493379');

    delete from public.course_udemy_bonus where course_id in ('7516a9d7-d1dd-42c8-8c5f-53cea00ed33c', '20a70350-dffd-40d5-87ad-a61e7360e743', 'd523ab0a-33e1-4928-8734-3956c6739d04', 'a626064a-7374-423e-86d6-1f8797f54a7c', '85a42f2c-5670-429b-8c72-f5a4e7494af2', 'e919197f-2908-5216-8c7b-0d4119158dbe', 'f42af617-4d01-4006-888b-4d6d6b6052f4', '74b2aa62-017d-4a09-88bc-1c1565e2b715', '1e73e4b8-99b3-40f3-8d02-fae509493379');

    -- Lessons are removed with their modules (on delete cascade).
    delete from public.course_modules where course_id in ('7516a9d7-d1dd-42c8-8c5f-53cea00ed33c', '20a70350-dffd-40d5-87ad-a61e7360e743', 'd523ab0a-33e1-4928-8734-3956c6739d04', 'a626064a-7374-423e-86d6-1f8797f54a7c', '85a42f2c-5670-429b-8c72-f5a4e7494af2', 'e919197f-2908-5216-8c7b-0d4119158dbe', 'f42af617-4d01-4006-888b-4d6d6b6052f4', '74b2aa62-017d-4a09-88bc-1c1565e2b715', '1e73e4b8-99b3-40f3-8d02-fae509493379');







  end if;
end $seed$;

-- Tools taught in each course (shown as cards on the course page). Replaces
-- the placeholder tools of these courses, once per database.
do $seed$ begin
  if not exists (select 1 from private.seed_log where name = 'catalogue-tools:2026-10-06') then
    delete from public.course_tools where course_id in ('7516a9d7-d1dd-42c8-8c5f-53cea00ed33c', '20a70350-dffd-40d5-87ad-a61e7360e743', 'd523ab0a-33e1-4928-8734-3956c6739d04', 'a626064a-7374-423e-86d6-1f8797f54a7c', '85a42f2c-5670-429b-8c72-f5a4e7494af2', 'e919197f-2908-5216-8c7b-0d4119158dbe', 'f42af617-4d01-4006-888b-4d6d6b6052f4', '74b2aa62-017d-4a09-88bc-1c1565e2b715', '1e73e4b8-99b3-40f3-8d02-fae509493379');
  end if;
end $seed$;

-- Cyber Security: Ethical Hacking, from its Udemy course (link added after the
-- parts above). Replaces its description, curriculum, Udemy bonus and tools,
-- once per database.
do $seed$ begin
  if not exists (select 1 from private.seed_log where name = 'catalogue-cyber:2026-10-06') then
    update public.courses set
      short_description = 'Learn ethical hacking and penetration testing in a safe lab, from Kali Linux and Nmap to Metasploit and web app security.',
      description = 'This course teaches how attackers work so that you can find and fix weaknesses before they are exploited. Everything is practised in your own virtual lab, on machines built to be vulnerable, and always within legal, authorised limits.

You set up Kali Linux in VirtualBox, learn the Linux command line and networking basics, then follow the five stages of a penetration test: reconnaissance, scanning with Nmap, vulnerability analysis with Nessus, exploitation with the Metasploit Framework, and post-exploitation. You also test web applications with Burp Suite for SQL injection, XSS, command injection and CSRF, and study man-in-the-middle attacks, wireless password cracking, Android security, anonymity and Active Directory.

Python runs through the whole course. You learn it from the basics and use it to write your own security tools, including a port scanner, a backdoor, a login brute-forcer and a hidden-directory finder.',
      curriculum_pdf_url = null
    where id = 'f7b2c938-f077-4b4c-8b37-73eb73e758f3';

    delete from public.course_udemy_bonus where course_id in ('f7b2c938-f077-4b4c-8b37-73eb73e758f3');

    delete from public.course_tools where course_id in ('f7b2c938-f077-4b4c-8b37-73eb73e758f3');

    delete from public.course_modules where course_id in ('f7b2c938-f077-4b4c-8b37-73eb73e758f3');


  end if;
end $seed$;

-- Frontend Development and Backend Development, each built from its half of the
-- MERN Udemy course (shared basics, JavaScript and Git in both). Replaces their
-- description, curriculum, Udemy bonus and tools, once per database.
do $seed$ begin
  if not exists (select 1 from private.seed_log where name = 'catalogue-web:2026-10-07') then
    update public.courses set
      short_description = 'Build modern, responsive interfaces with HTML, CSS, Tailwind, JavaScript, React and Next.js.',
      description = 'This course covers everything that happens in the browser, from your first HTML page to complete applications built with React and Next.js. It starts from the basics, so no coding experience is needed.

You begin with how the web works, then learn HTML, CSS and Tailwind CSS, practising each with hands-on challenges. The JavaScript modules cover the language from the ground up: data types, functions, objects and classes, the DOM, and asynchronous code with promises and async/await, followed by small projects such as a to-do app, an expense tracker and a quiz. You also learn Git and GitHub.

The second half is React and Next.js. You build ten React projects covering hooks, routing and the Context API, then use Next.js to build full applications: an authentication system, a Q&A site with Appwrite and Zustand, an AI-powered SaaS app, and a browser-based code editor.',
      curriculum_pdf_url = null
    where id = 'a31d768d-750b-4607-8c8d-6cd1a8b5994b';

    update public.courses set
      short_description = 'Build secure APIs and server applications with Node.js, Express, MongoDB, SQL, Docker and deployment.',
      description = 'This course teaches the server side of web development: building APIs, designing databases, securing applications and putting them into production. It starts with the JavaScript you need, so no backend experience is required.

After the JavaScript fundamentals and Git, you learn how Node.js works and build complete backends with Express and MongoDB: project structure, authentication with JWT access and refresh tokens, email verification, file uploads, role-based permissions and aggregation pipelines. You also learn SQL with PostgreSQL and MySQL, from table design and normalisation to joins, and move on to ORMs such as Prisma and Drizzle.

Later modules cover the Fastify framework, event-driven architecture with webhooks, a secure learning management system with a payment gateway, Docker containers, and deploying to your own VPS with Nginx and SSL.',
      curriculum_pdf_url = null
    where id = '8ddf1088-14f1-46d0-827a-17b814c7539f';

    delete from public.course_udemy_bonus where course_id in ('a31d768d-750b-4607-8c8d-6cd1a8b5994b', '8ddf1088-14f1-46d0-827a-17b814c7539f');

    delete from public.course_tools where course_id in ('a31d768d-750b-4607-8c8d-6cd1a8b5994b', '8ddf1088-14f1-46d0-827a-17b814c7539f');

    delete from public.course_modules where course_id in ('a31d768d-750b-4607-8c8d-6cd1a8b5994b', '8ddf1088-14f1-46d0-827a-17b814c7539f');


  end if;
end $seed$;
